# AMYGO RaaS Engineering Core

1. Before changing code, list affected modules, files, interfaces, databases, risks, and tests.
2. Do not mix large refactors and new features in the same PR.
3. Vendor APIs, SDKs, DTOs, and error codes may only live in the corresponding Adapter module.
4. Domain layer must not depend on PUDU, KEENON, Unitree, Zeus, or other vendor types.
5. Do not globally rename Car→Robot or Order→Task from Legacy.
6. Every robot command must include commandId, correlationId, tenantId, siteId, robotId, expiresAt, idempotencyKey, and actor.
7. Duplicate commands, duplicate webhooks, out-of-order events, timeouts, and restarts must be handled safely.
8. Cloud must never send speed, steering angle, joint angles, torque, or continuous low-level motion control.
9. High-risk human actions, permission/asset/config changes must write Audit Log.
10. All business reads/writes must enforce tenant/site isolation; never trust request-body tenantId as authority.
11. Database changes only via versioned migrations; no manual production edits.
12. Legacy changes require Characterization Tests first.
13. New API/event/DB changes must update OpenAPI/schema/sample/contract tests.
14. Never commit secrets, tokens, certificates, customer PII, or production logs.
15. Do not invent vendor APIs; without formal docs only implement Port/Mock/open questions.
16. Unsupported capabilities must return CAPABILITY_NOT_SUPPORTED explicitly.
17. End of task: run build, unit, integration, contract, lint, and migration checks when applicable.
18. Output must include changed files, behavior diff, test evidence, open issues, and rollback approach.
